WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
In Italy we have a famous song:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:12.240
In case the World is falling down, I go back&nbsp;
a little bit to not get hurt. But what if an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.640
nuclear bomb were to fall on the City where&nbsp;
I live in Tuscany (which is Prato)? This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:23.840
something I ask myself with a bit of paranoia.&nbsp;
How much "further back" am I supposed to ensure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:31.120
I don't vaporize instantly? After all, the&nbsp;
dogma of this era seems to be "never say never":&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:37.360
pandemics, wars, Italy out of the World&nbsp;
Cup. Meanwhile, everyone wants to build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.720
their own bunker. Yes, there are companies that&nbsp;
specialize in this. Now you know. In Switzerland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:50.000
just to say, since 1963 it is mandatory by law&nbsp;
to provide every building with a bomb shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.600
while in Italy we don't have any regulatory&nbsp;
plan providing for the construction of bunkers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:02.240
At least in theory. But, hey, what’s the deal.&nbsp;
We can always use our cellars as bunkers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:10.320
After getting all the permissions, of course.&nbsp;
However, since a bunker costs several tens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.280
thousands of dollars and since I am not paid&nbsp;
enough, if an atomic bomb were to fall on my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.920
little town, Prato, I would have no choice&nbsp;
but to run away. Hopefully with a fast car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.560
Luckily for me, a simulator, Nukemap, created&nbsp;
by historian Alex Wellerstein, has been around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.200
for several years now, showing the range of&nbsp;
action, and destruction, of an atomic device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.520
We'll take a look at it, but before I give you&nbsp;
any unjustified anxiety, I wanted to ask myself:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.440
what are the nations that possess the warheads&nbsp;
capable to unleash the atomic holocaust?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.840
These are not so many, and the so funny "club of&nbsp;
the atom" is currently limited to nine members: on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.520
the one hand you have the " classic" United&nbsp;
States, Russia, France, the United Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.200
China, all of the signatories of the Treaty&nbsp;
on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.560
but on the other hand you have 4 countries&nbsp;
that are not yet members of such agreement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.480
namely India, Pakistan, North Korea and Israel,&nbsp;
even if the latter is only unofficially part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.680
it. Apart from a couple of them, they all&nbsp;
seem to be nice and quiet. But surprise:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:22.560
we Italians too have nuclear warheads at our&nbsp;
disposal. Oh well, they are not really ours.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.400
According to the NATO nuclear sharing plan, it has&nbsp;
been decided to involve in the "nuclear warfare"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.560
also some "non-nuclear" countries&nbsp;
of the alliance like us italians.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:39.360
Shared strategies and planning, mostly, but also&nbsp;
supply of warheads. So much non proliferation...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.080
I can smell it. The United States (and who&nbsp;
otherwise?) have lent Italy, Belgium, Germany,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:52.000
the Netherlands and Turkey their own toys that,&nbsp;
of course, we all cannot use at our pleasure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.720
You all understand? Don't play with those gifts.&nbsp;
The bombs are guarded by U.S. soldiers and without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:04.720
U.S. codes they can't be used. But in case of&nbsp;
war, we still have to prove that we are capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:10.000
of using them, and we cannot afford to fall&nbsp;
off the wagon. According to a report by analyst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.200
Hans Kristensen, of the Natural Resources Defense&nbsp;
Council, in 2005 in Italy there were 90 warheads:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:23.200
50 in the base of Aviano and 40 in the base&nbsp;
of Ghedi Torre. Today the estimates point a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.880
total of forty warheads, but it seems also to&nbsp;
be a real secret bilateral agreement between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:35.040
our country and the United States, called Stone&nbsp;
Ax, which would provide for a further deployment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.880
of American nuclear weapons on our territory.&nbsp;
Making an estimate of the warheads currently in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:48.160
circulation is a bit complicated but one thing&nbsp;
is certain: Russia and the USA share about 90%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.760
of the world's nuclear weapons. According&nbsp;
to the Federation of American Scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:02.640
in the first part of 2022 the estimated number&nbsp;
of warheads around the world is 12.700. Of these,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:09.440
except those being dismantled, the actual&nbsp;
warheads for military use are 9400,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:18.400
but only 3700 are the ones currently deployed&nbsp;
and operational, 2000 even in "state of alert",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:26.000
ready for immediate use. Russia would be in&nbsp;
the first place with 5977 warheads, followed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:33.920
the United States with 5 thousand 428, but if we&nbsp;
take into account only the deployed warheads, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:43.840
United States would have a slight advantage: 1744&nbsp;
against 1588. Just to understand the difference in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:50.880
level with the rest of the world, in third place&nbsp;
China boasts "only" three hundred fifty warheads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:58.400
up to 20 of North Korea. You have to eat more&nbsp;
uranium, Dear Kim. But we should go easy on good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:04.320
old Kim, apparently he has some very dangerous new&nbsp;
toys now. In fact, Pyongyang's latest tests have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:10.720
glorified the power of the new Hwasong 17 missiles&nbsp;
capable of reaching American and European soil.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.000
Of course, so far they have not gone further&nbsp;
than Japan. A coincidence, one might say.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:47.840
Okay, potentially Kim could hit us right now. What&nbsp;
about the others? France would have no problem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.560
hit their beloved cousins from Italy and since&nbsp;
in the past they have already given us their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.440
warheads (Zidane World Cup head scene) I would&nbsp;
be careful. Also USA and UK may have no problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:03.440
to send us their missiles and neither Russia.&nbsp;
Pakistan and India perhaps would not make it: both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:09.600
the Pakistani Shaheen and the Indian Agni have a&nbsp;
more limited range. After all they only care about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:16.640
destroying each other and maybe hitting China.&nbsp;
China, with its DF-41 missiles and especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.800
with the new hypersonic models, (when they'll be&nbsp;
ready for use), has all the requirements to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:26.400
good candidate to destroy my town in Tuscany.&nbsp;
Come on, bring it on. You and what army? Mh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:37.040
they sound convincing. So, what would happen if a&nbsp;
nuclear warhead fell right here in the exact spot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.880
where I live? Let's say for example, a Russian&nbsp;
warhead hits the ground right here. Purely random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.080
example. First of all, according to the experts&nbsp;
of the Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists, it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:53.440
to be believed that the nuclear warheads today at&nbsp;
the disposal of the Russians are around a charge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:07:01.120
of 800 kilotons which, to be clear, would be&nbsp;
equivalent to 800 thousand tons of dynamite. Those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:08.080
of hiroshima and Nagasaki were between 15 and 20&nbsp;
kilotons. Intercepting a nuclear Intercontinental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:13.600
ballistic missile is technically possible, but&nbsp;
very difficult and unpredictable, given the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:20.560
parabolic trajectory of the ICBM. The most basic&nbsp;
system is basically just shooting a missile at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:25.920
the missile. During the Cold War, that’s what&nbsp;
Russians and Americans called “Anti-ballistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:32.800
missile”. But we never had the honor to experiment&nbsp;
the effectiveness of this tactic so far. Hiroshima&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:38.720
and Nagasaki were the only two history cases&nbsp;
of nukes dropped on civilians, and Japan didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:46.320
have any anti-ballistic missile at that time. The&nbsp;
idea would be to hit the ICBM and make it blow up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.520
somewhere other than its intended target. This&nbsp;
with all the consequences it may have on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.880
atmosphere. Anti-ballistic systems are present&nbsp;
in various countries and are still under full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:02.640
development. Nowadays, India’s ABM system is&nbsp;
capable of intercepting missiles up to two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:09.120
thousand six hundred km and potentially to&nbsp;
five thousand km. In a war scenario, no one has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.840
activated their own defense system. Yet. And so,&nbsp;
we can only speculate. In a report by the American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.800
Physical Society Panel on Public Affairs,&nbsp;
even the Americans seems to have a limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:24.240
capability to intercept an intercontinental&nbsp;
balistic missile. In this study it is stated:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:29.280
“the current capabilities are low and will likely&nbsp;
continue to be low for the next 15 years”. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.920
strikes from North Korea against the US are not&nbsp;
fully prevented yet. And we are speaking about 20&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:41.280
warheads. Imagine six thousands Russian nukes.&nbsp;
Goodbye Sirs. Proposed by the Administration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.960
The U.S. Ground-Based Midcourse Defense, also&nbsp;
known as GMD, is operational in both Alaska&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.920
and California and provides more protection&nbsp;
against the Nuclear threat from North Korean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:57.280
missiles or launches from Russia or China,&nbsp;
but is likely less effective against missiles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:03.680
launched from the Middle East. Here in Italy&nbsp;
are developing the Aster 30 Block II system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:10.080
with a range of three thousand km. In the meantime&nbsp;
we need to survive without it and look for two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:16.480
NATO defense sites, one in Romania, the other&nbsp;
one in Poland. This means only one thing: boom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.360
Detonated a few hundred meters above Piazza&nbsp;
del Duomo – I Hope Our Dear Bishop forgives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:30.400
me- the explosion would generate a ball of&nbsp;
fire and hot air, of millions of degrees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:36.800
Fahrenheit, that would instantly vaporize&nbsp;
everything within a radius of 880 meters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.560
for an area of about 2 square kilometers. The&nbsp;
shockwave will then spread fatally within an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:49.040
area of 14 square kilometers from the explosion&nbsp;
site, severely damaging and razing most buildings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:54.960
to the ground. In general, anyone who manages&nbsp;
to survive within a radius of 2 kilometers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:01.120
380 - which includes me - will have a short time&nbsp;
because the radiation will prove fatal within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:08.320
a month. at 4 km and 760 meters The buildings&nbsp;
from the explosion will report moderate damage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:14.960
but the risk of fire will be high though. At a&nbsp;
distance of 11 km and 400 meters, for a total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:23.440
area of 409 kilometers so well beyond Prato up to&nbsp;
municipalities such as Sesto Fiorentino, Signa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:29.520
Campi Bisenzio, Poggio a Caiano and Carmignano&nbsp;
(but not the much hated city of Pistoia ...), the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:37.120
hot air will cause third degree burns but you will&nbsp;
not even feel them, it is very likely that your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:43.200
pain receptor nerves will be already fatally&nbsp;
damaged. Finally, the explosion will affect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:49.440
a total area of 4 hundred seventy seven square&nbsp;
km around the Cathedral of Prato and depending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:55.360
on where the wind will blow, there will be a&nbsp;
radioactive rain of one hundred eighty one km,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:00.133
which will affect at different intensity a&nbsp;
total area of four thousand square km. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.133 --> 00:11:01.360
mushroom cloud on the ashes of Prato will be 19&nbsp;
km high, with a radius of the head of 25 km. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:06.480
if I wanted to save myself at least from the&nbsp;
damage of the explosion, I would have to move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:15.520
at least 12 km from the center of Prato. I could&nbsp;
be safe in Florence and yes, even in Pistoia. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:22.880
from Prato have some long lasting disputes with&nbsp;
those in Pistoia. In case you're luckier than me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:28.240
you could always live near a large "public"&nbsp;
fallout shelter. The luckiest ones in Italy live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:34.000
in the province of Verona, in Affi, where there&nbsp;
is the largest bunker of its kind in our country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:40.160
located in the bowels of Mount Moscal. Built&nbsp;
in the Sixties to house a NATO command post,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:46.400
it is 13 thousand square meters wide and&nbsp;
can accommodate almost 1000 people. Once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:53.040
well-stocked, for some years now it has&nbsp;
been dismantled and is now almost unusable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:07.920
You can also try it in Trentino, under Mount Mais&nbsp;
in Val di Non, where you will find the Gampen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:15.440
Bunker. Being bombed during World War II, our&nbsp;
country has hundreds if not thousands of shelters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:20.080
from private to public shelters. In nearby&nbsp;
Florence you could look for one of the many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:25.520
city shelters built to escape from the bombings:&nbsp;
from the undergrounds of the Basilica of San&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:31.120
Lorenzo to Palazzo Vecchio. If you find yourself&nbsp;
in Florence during a nuclear attack, observe on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:37.040
the walls the presence of an R, indicating the&nbsp;
proximity to a bunker. In Torino, then, under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:42.946
Piazza del Risorgimento, there is still an active&nbsp;
shelter capable of accommodating one thousand one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.946 --> 00:12:47.200
hundred fifty people, though during the war&nbsp;
it happened to welcome twice as many people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:53.920
Just as in Naples, the population found refuge&nbsp;
from bombing in the network of nineteenth-century&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.920 --> 00:13:00.000
tunnels built by the Bourbons. Famous in Milan&nbsp;
are shelter 87, under an elementary school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.840
and the network of Breda&nbsp;
bunkers in the Parco Nord.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:17.760
In Rome, Mussolini and Savoia had their&nbsp;
own bunkers with blackjack and hookers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:23.280
Today you won't exactly find this luxury&nbsp;
in the bunker under the park of Villa Ada,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:28.800
once a Royal Residence wanted by King Vittorio&nbsp;
Emanuele the Third. You will find instead an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:35.440
anonymous and disturbing parking lot. Mussolini&nbsp;
had two bunkers, one under Palazzo venezia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:41.080
and another at Villa torlonia, both in&nbsp;
Rome, but they were not even completed. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:48.240
45 km from Rome, in the meanders of Mount Soratte&nbsp;
in the proximity of the town of Sant'Oreste,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:54.640
you can find a vast tangle of underground&nbsp;
tunnels, long 4 km and designed to accommodate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.640 --> 00:14:00.400
the highest charges of the army. These tunnels&nbsp;
were then partially converted into a bomb shelter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:06.720
by NATO during the Cold War. Yet, if some&nbsp;
ill-intentioned nation wants to attack us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:11.760
we should expect more than anything else a&nbsp;
direct bombing towards military installations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:17.200
such as Aviano and Ghedi, with consequences&nbsp;
that Nukemap itself refuses to consider.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:25.120
I apologize if I too have provided you with&nbsp;
a daily dose of atomic anxiety. Just in case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:31.840
remember your potassium Iodide pills for radiation&nbsp;
and Nukemap in your hand to calculate the damage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:38.240
and the probability of survival. An advice: DO&nbsp;
NOT simulate the explosion of the Tsar bomb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:42.880
the most powerful ever built and designed&nbsp;
by Russia. You may experience nightmares.

